flyExplorer
===========

flyExplorer is a Windows file manager. The canonical product on `main` is now
the C++/WinRT WinUI 3 application under `app/winui`.

Quick start
-----------

Build Release:

    build.bat Release

Run the built product:

    run.bat Release

Open a specific folder:

    run.bat Release D:\

Run source/contract checks:

    test.bat source

Clean generated build output without touching source or evidence logs:

    clean.bat build

Remove the local package cache too (packages will be restored on next build):

    clean.bat all

Run the full owned Debug + Release validation sequence:

    python -X utf8 tools\winui\run_checks.py full

Canonical repository layout
---------------------------

    app/winui/        WinUI 3 application, XAML, helper and project templates
    src/base/         UI-independent native core reused by the WinUI product
    tests/winui/      source contracts, owned GUI tests and native fixtures
    tools/winui/      canonical local build/test orchestration
    docs/             current and historical engineering documentation
    out/              ignored build products/intermediates
    .cache/nuget/     ignored NuGet cache
    logs/             ignored local validation evidence

The old `experiments/phase6_winui_shell` product path no longer exists. Phase6
is the product, so it lives under `app/winui`.

Build outputs
-------------

Build products are intentionally kept out of `app/winui`.

Release executable:

    out\winui\Release\FlyExplorerWinUIShell.exe

Debug executable:

    out\winui\Debug\FlyExplorerWinUIShell.exe

Do not copy only the EXE; the sibling WinUI resources and
`FlyShellIsolationHelper.exe` are part of the runtime set.

Retired MFC
-----------

The previous MFC default exists only in Git history at `cbffb48`.
No MFC source, build, distribution, library or runnable legacy test tree is
retained in the current checkout. Exact old-product recovery/rebuild must use
that historical commit in a separate worktree. Phase5 remains retired.

Development status
------------------

See `docs/development/CURRENT_STATUS.md` for accepted functionality and open
release gates. GitHub Actions remain opt-in/manual according to project policy;
local commands above do not publish releases or change the default application.

